identifiability.synthetic_recovery.reason:
Recovery: 200 labelled synthetic datasets were generated at the real design and fitted noise (seed_base 90210) from distinct f_L ∝ x^0.35, f_M ∝ x^1, f_S ∝ x^0.6, then refit with M2. Results:
- per-curve median relative error: f_L 0.022 [0.004, 0.078], f_M 0.034, f_S 0.026;
- 95% band widths are logged;
- the L−M contrast is recovered at 0.198 [0.139, 0.249] vs a true 0.196, with the correct sign 100% of the time;
- ρ is recovered at 0.589 [0.319, 0.812] vs 0.6.

What is and is not discriminable is mapped under seven generators: opponent 94% correct, fitted cone 91% (delta CI includes 0), K2-cone 80%, and K2-CIELAB vs LCh indistinguishable by identity.

Caveats: there is only one strong recovery generator, and the power simulations use 1 CV repeat and 6 restarts.

