failure_analysis.specificity.reason:
The items name concrete regimes with evidence:
- weak cross-dataset identification by design;
- Ekman's two-decade S range, motivating the per-dataset scaling, with a rerun without it;
- the outer/inner curvature trade, with ρ varying across bases;
- CIs of about ±0.2 nats/rating on 45+91 pairs, too wide for M2−M1 and K2−M1;
- L1-only aggregation;
- residual DR/curvature aliasing in cone-space arc length;
- CIELAB ΔL* ≡ 0 for Ekman, which lowers effective complexity;
